    <div class="vk-intro__content">
      <span class="vk-intro__eyebrow">Why V-Kool &amp; Window Film Philadelphia</span>
      <h2 class="vk-intro__title">V-Kool VK70 Is in the Guggenheim and the AIA Headquarters. Philadelphia Properties Deserve the Same.</h2>
      <p class="vk-intro__lead">V-Kool window film in Philadelphia is available through Window Film Philadelphia across the VK75, VK70, VK55, and VK40 spectrally selective series. V-Kool's approach to solar control is different from every ceramic or dyed film on the market: where ceramic films absorb infrared heat and make the glass warm, V-Kool's multi-layer sputtered films reflect it. The glass stays cooler. Less secondary heat radiates into the room. The VK70 flagship — with 70% VLT, 55% TSER, and 94% infrared rejection — has been chosen for the AIA Headquarters in Washington D.C. and the Guggenheim Museum in New York.</p>
      <p class="vk-intro__body">V-Kool window tint Philadelphia properties receive is manufactured to NFRC standards and backed by a lifetime residential warranty and a 10-year commercial warranty — the full Eastman warranty infrastructure that comes with every authorized installation. The VK series has been tested independently and its performance data is compared to NFRC.org official ratings, giving specifiers, architects, and property owners the apples-to-apples comparison data they need.</p>
