    <div class="vk-why__content">
      <span class="vk-why__eyebrow">Why V-Kool for Philadelphia</span>
      <h2 class="vk-why__headline">V-Kool's Multi-Layer Sputtered Films Reflect Philadelphia's Heat. Every Other Film Absorbs It.</h2>
      <p class="vk-why__intro">
        Every solar control film reduces heat — the question is how. Dyed and ceramic films absorb infrared radiation, which makes the glass itself hot. V-Kool's multi-layer spectrally selective construction, as detailed at <a href="https://v-kool-usa.com/products/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="vk-body-link">V-Kool USA</a>, targets the infrared portion of sunlight far more than visible light — so heat is rejected while the room stays bright. The VK70 flagship delivers 70% VLT, 55% TSER, and 94% infrared rejection at only ~9% exterior reflectance. As a V-Kool film installer for Philadelphia commercial and residential properties, Window Film Philadelphia specifies from the full VK series based on each building's orientation, glazing type, and performance targets.
      </p>
      <ul class="vk-why__bullets">
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>V-Kool spectrally selective films reflect infrared radiation — where ceramic films absorb heat and make the glass hot, V-Kool glass stays cool to the touch</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
