      <h3 class="vk-pl-row__heading">V-KOOL 75 — Maximum Daylight Transmission for Philadelphia's Historic and High-Clarity Glass</h3>
      <p class="vk-pl-row__body">V-KOOL 75 (VK75) delivers the highest visible light transmission in the V-Kool series — 77% VLT — making it the right specification when preserving maximum daylight is the primary requirement and some reduction in solar heat rejection is acceptable. For Philadelphia's historic district properties in Society Hill, Old City, and Chestnut Hill, where preservation guidelines restrict anything that visibly changes the glass, VK75 is effectively invisible while still providing meaningful UV and infrared protection.</p>
      <p class="vk-pl-row__body">VK75 is also the specification for north-facing glass and interior spaces where daylighting is already limited and any reduction in visible light would materially worsen the occupant experience. With 77.14% infrared rejection and 99% UV block, VK75 still outperforms most ceramic solar control films on heat rejection while maintaining a level of clarity that reads as untreated glass from any practical viewing distance.</p>
