      <h3 class="vk-pl-row__heading">V-KOOL 55 — Balanced Performance for Philadelphia Properties That Need to Meet SHGC Requirements</h3>
      <p class="vk-pl-row__body">V-KOOL 55 (VK55) sits between VK70 and VK40 in the series — with 58% VLT, 59% TSER, and 96% infrared rejection, it was specifically developed to meet the International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) requirement of a Solar Heat Gain Coefficient of 0.40. For Philadelphia commercial renovation projects that must demonstrate energy code compliance, VK55 provides the specifiable performance threshold while maintaining a significantly higher VLT than darker tint films at the same SHGC.</p>
      <p class="vk-pl-row__body">For south- and west-facing Philadelphia office glass where the afternoon solar load is the primary driver and moderate privacy is a secondary benefit, VK55 delivers measurably better heat rejection than VK70 while preserving a comfortable, daylit interior. The 58% visible light transmission reads as lightly tinted glass rather than dark solar film, which keeps the building's exterior appearance consistent with Philadelphia's architectural standards for commercial glazing on most streets.</p>
