      <h3 class="vk-pl-row__heading">V-KOOL 40 — Maximum Heat and Glare Control for Philadelphia's Highest-Load Exposures</h3>
      <p class="vk-pl-row__body">V-KOOL 40 (VK40) is the performance leader in the V-Kool series — with 64.53% TSER and 98.3% infrared rejection, it delivers the most aggressive heat control in the lineup while maintaining 42.8% visible light transmission. At that VLT level, the glass reads as lightly tinted rather than dark, preserving meaningful natural light even as it blocks nearly all of the infrared heat spectrum. VK40 is the specification when glare reduction and maximum heat control are the primary drivers and some visible tinting is acceptable.</p>
      <p class="vk-pl-row__body">For Philadelphia's west-facing commercial glass — the Category 1 solar load exposure that creates afternoon hotspots on Center City office floors from noon onward — VK40 resolves the heat problem more completely than any other product in the series. For residential applications in rowhomes facing a western or southern orientation where afternoon sun makes rooms uncomfortable even after VK70 installation, VK40 provides the additional performance margin that closes the gap.</p>
