<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="vk-faq" id="faq">
  <div class="vk-faq__inner">
    <div class="vk-faq__header fade-in">
      <span class="vk-eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="vk-faq__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p>Honest answers about V-Kool window film in Philadelphia from specialists with over 15 years of installation experience.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="vk-faq__cta-btn">Talk to a Specialist</a>
    </div>
    <div class="vk-faq__list fade-in">
      <div class="vk-faq__item vk-faq__item--open">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>What is V-Kool window film?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>V-Kool is a premium window film brand owned by Eastman. For architectural applications, the V-Kool lineup includes VK75, VK70, VK55, and VK40 — all spectrally selective, all NFRC-tested, and all built on V-Kool's multi-layer sputtered technology. VK70 is the flagship; VK75 maximizes daylight; VK55 meets SHGC .40 code; VK40 delivers maximum heat and glare control.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>What is XIR® technology and how is it different from ceramic film?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>XIR® is V-Kool's proprietary sputtering technology. Where dyed and ceramic films absorb infrared heat — making the glass itself hot — V-Kool's sputtered films reflect infrared radiation rather than absorbing it. This means the glass stays cooler and less secondary radiant heat enters the room. The sputtering process deposits microscopic layers of precious metals onto the film at V-Kool's ISO-9001 certified plant in Dresden, Germany.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>What is the VK70?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>V-KOOL 70 is the flagship of the series — 70% VLT, 55% TSER, 94% IR rejection, ~9% exterior reflectance. It's the film chosen by the AIA headquarters and the Guggenheim Museum. For Philadelphia commercial buildings and premium residences where both clarity and comfort are required, VK70 is the standard recommendation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>Does V-Kool window film interfere with Wi-Fi or cellular signals?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>V-Kool's V-Kool spectrally selective films are non-metallic in their visible-spectrum construction, which minimizes signal interference. This is a meaningful advantage for dense Philadelphia commercial floors with extensive wireless infrastructure — Center City tech tenants and financial services firms specifically benefit from this characteristic compared to conventional metallic reflective films.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>Is V-Kool window film worth it for Philadelphia's climate?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>Philadelphia's IECC Zone 4A climate creates a genuine year-round demand for solar control. In summer, V-Kool VK70 reduces solar heat gain on south- and west-facing glass. In winter, the low-emissivity properties of V-Kool's sputtered films help retain interior heat. That combination makes V-Kool a strong year-round specification for Philadelphia commercial and residential properties.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>What UV protection does V-Kool provide?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>V-Kool V-Kool films have earned the Skin Cancer Foundation's Seal of Recommendation for UV protection performance. All V-Kool product lines block 99%+ of harmful UV radiation that causes fading in flooring, furniture, artwork, and merchandise. For Philadelphia properties with south-facing glass exposure and valuable interior finishes, V-Kool's UV block is a meaningful asset protection benefit.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>How do I choose between VK75, VK70, VK55, and VK40?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>VK75 (77% VLT) is the choice when maximum daylight is the priority and historic preservation matters. VK70 (70% VLT) is the flagship — most buildings choose this first. VK55 (58% VLT) is specified when energy code compliance (SHGC .40) is required or when west-facing load needs more aggressive control. VK40 (42.8% VLT) delivers the maximum TSER of 64.5% for the highest heat and glare loads. Window Film Philadelphia will recommend the right film after assessing your glass orientation and building type.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>Are V-Kool films HOA and historic district compatible?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>Yes. VK70 and VK75 have approximately 9% exterior reflectance — well below the threshold that most HOA guidelines and Philadelphia historic preservation rules restrict. The near-neutral appearance of both films means they read as clear glass from the street, making them appropriate for Society Hill, Old City, Chestnut Hill, and other neighborhoods with appearance restrictions on window treatments.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>Can V-Kool window film be installed on existing Philadelphia glass?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>Yes. V-Kool films are applied to the interior glass surface of existing windows — no glass replacement required. Window Film Philadelphia assesses glass type, orientation, and performance goals before recommending a product series to ensure compatibility, including insulated glass units common in Center City commercial buildings.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="vk-faq__item">
        <div class="vk-faq__q"><span>Where is V-Kool manufactured?</span><span class="vk-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="vk-faq__a"><p>V-Kool window films are manufactured at an ISO-9001 certified plant in Dresden, Germany — one of a small number of facilities worldwide capable of the precision multi-layer sputtering process that XIR® technology requires. The sputtering technology was developed in Silicon Valley, USA. V-Kool is owned by Eastman Chemical Company, the same parent as LLumar and Vista.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

